# {{name}}

A web app built with [Ironhold](https://github.com/ironhold-rs/ironhold): secure by default, with sign up, log in and log out ready to go.

## Run it

```bash
ironhold dev
```

This builds the app, starts it at <http://127.0.0.1:3000>, and rebuilds and restarts it whenever you save a file. If a change doesn't compile, the last working version keeps running. You can also use `cargo run`.

{{database_notes}}

## Test

```bash
cargo test
```

Tests drive the app like a browser with `ironhold::testing::TestClient`.

## Project layout

| Path | What's in it |
|---|---|
| `src/lib.rs` | Routes |
| `src/auth.rs` | Sign up, log in, log out |
| `src/pages.rs` | Pages |
| `src/user.rs` | Users and their queries |
| `src/layout.rs` | The shared page layout |
| `migrations/` | Database migrations, applied on startup |
| `tests/` | Tests |

## Configuration

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | Where the database is |
| `IRONHOLD_ENV` | `development` or `production` |
| `IRONHOLD_ADDR` | Listen address (default `127.0.0.1:3000`) |
| `RUST_LOG` | Log level, e.g. `info` or `debug` |

`ironhold dev` reads these from `.env` (see `.env.example`).

## Deploy

```bash
cargo build --release
```

That produces one binary, `target/release/{{name}}`, with migrations built in. Run it with `IRONHOLD_ENV=production` and `IRONHOLD_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8080` behind an HTTPS proxy such as Caddy or Nginx. HTTPS is required in production: session cookies are only sent over HTTPS.
